* mmbt5401.lib - Diodes Incorporated MMBT5401, high-voltage PNP, SOT-23.
* VENDOR MODEL, COPIED VERBATIM FROM THE MANUFACTURER'S OWN FILE.
*
* USAGE:
*   .include models/bjt_pnp/mmbt5401.lib
*   Q1 collector base emitter MMBT5401
*
* Role in this project: the VAS transistor of the gain block
* (circuits/preamp/gain_block.py:316), one instance per block. With the
* 470 pF Miller capacitor it sets the DOMINANT POLE of the whole
* amplifier, which is why ADR-017 kept this die instead of looking for a
* "better" transistor: a genuinely different device here moves a figure
* the topology is built on.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* THE PART THE PROJECT BUYS IS THE MMBT5401, NOT THE 2N5401
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* Same die, SOT-23 instead of TO-92. onsemi publishes no reachable SPICE
* model for the 2N5401 (its /download/models/lib/2n5401.lib is the soft
* 404 of docs/limitations.md #18 - re-falsified in L24, not inherited);
* Diodes publishes one for the MMBT5401. T7 (ADR-016) requires a
* manufacturer model, so the project follows the manufacturer that has
* one. Two consequences ADR-017 states rather than hides: the dissipation
* budget drops from 625 mW to 310 mW on the minimum recommended pad
* (against a worst case of 86.3 mW at the real operating point, margin
* 3.6x), and BVceo drops from 160 V to 150 V (against 30 V worst case).
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* PROVENANCE - the short version. Full record in
* models/bjt_pnp/mmbt5401.provenance.json, the freeze in
* vendor/bjt_pnp/diodes_inc/MMBT5401/PROVENANCE.json, and the reasoning
* in docs/preamp/reports/2026-09-10-L24-t7-dispositivi-attivi.md
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* Unlike models/jfet/lsk489.lib and models/bjt_pnp/ls350.lib, this model
* was NOT transcribed: Diodes serves it as a text file, so it was frozen
* byte-for-byte at
* vendor/bjt_pnp/diodes_inc/MMBT5401/MMBT5401.spice.txt and copied here
* unchanged. NOTHING WAS REMOVED - not even the mfg= that had to be
* stripped from the two Linear Systems models, because this file has
* none. No value was rounded, reordered or "corrected". The vendor's own
* AS-IS warranty disclaimer is reproduced below unaltered, as license
* traceability.
*
* The property is checkable, not asserted:
*
*   diff <(grep -v '^\*' vendor/bjt_pnp/diodes_inc/MMBT5401/MMBT5401.spice.txt) \
*        <(grep -v '^\*' models/bjt_pnp/mmbt5401.lib)      # empty
*
* WHERE THE FILE CAME FROM, and why the URL alone would not have been
* enough: on diodes.com the path of a model is decided ONLY by its id -
* the part name in the URL is not checked by the server, so a request can
* name one part and receive another (docs/limitations.md #21). The truth
* is in the name= of the Content-Type. This file was checked that way and
* by reading its own header.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* PSPICE QUASI-SATURATION PARAMETERS: ngspice ACCEPTS THEM SILENTLY
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* The model carries QUASIMOD=1, RCO=14 and GAMMA=1.5E-8, which are PSpice
* quasi-saturation parameters. ngspice 47 emits ZERO warnings on this
* file - re-verified in L25 by running it, not inherited from L24.
*
* That silence is only meaningful because the comparison exists: on
* models/jfet/lsk489.lib the same ngspice prints FOUR "unrecognized
* parameter ... ignored" lines. When it does not know a parameter, it
* says so. So the absence of a warning here is evidence that the
* parameters were taken, not evidence that nobody looked.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* CROSS-CHECKED AGAINST THE DATASHEET - SIX OF SIX INSIDE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* Datasheet DS30057 Rev. 12-2 (c) 2024, revision read from the footer,
* frozen at vendor/bjt_pnp/diodes_inc/MMBT5401/MMBT5401.pdf. Measured
* with ngspice 47 at the datasheet's own conditions, set temp = 25 (the
* datasheet is @ 25 C; ngspice defaults to 27, and XTB = 1.5 makes hFE
* temperature dependent, so the default would shift every number here):
*
*   hFE   @ IC = -10 mA, VCE = -5 V     124.917    window 60 .. 240   INSIDE
*   fT    @ IC = -10 mA, VCE = -10 V,
*         ftest = 100 MHz               160.116 MHz   100 MHz MIN.    INSIDE
*   C_obo @ VCB = -10 V, 1 MHz, IE = 0  3.7063 pF     6 pF MAX.       INSIDE
*
* This is, with the MMBT5551, the only model in this repo whose every
* checked quantity lands inside the manufacturer's own window. The
* LSK489 has NC-013, the LS352 has NC-020, the two MJE have NC-024 and
* NC-025.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* THE fT FIGURE CORRECTS L24, AND THE CAUSE IS THE BIAS CURRENT
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* L24 and ADR-017 record fT = 169.5 MHz. This file locks 160.116 MHz,
* and the difference is NOT a disagreement about the model: it is the
* operating point the two measurements were taken at.
*
* fT was re-measured in L25 with the collector current VERIFIED at the
* datasheet's own IC = 10.000 mA (op prints -1.00000e-02 exactly), and
* the answer is 160.1 MHz on three agreeing legs: the datasheet's own
* definition - |hfe| at ftest = 100 MHz, times 100 MHz - gives 160.116
* MHz, the |hfe| = 1 crossing gives 160.084 MHz, and the gain-bandwidth
* product at 50 MHz gives 160.098 MHz. A plateau, not a slope, so on
* THIS device the choice of definition is worth 0.02%.
*
* L24's 169.5 MHz is reproduced EXACTLY by driving a round IB = 100 uA
* instead, which this model turns into IC = 12.68 mA - 27% above the
* current the datasheet specifies fT at. Measured, not guessed: the same
* deck at IB = 100 uA returns 169.4698 MHz.
*
* The VERDICT does not change - both numbers clear the 100 MHz minimum -
* but the number does, by -5.5%, and it is the number that feeds the
* dominant-pole discussion. It is the same trap ADR-017 itself warns
* about one line later ("attenzione a QUALE corrente"), caught on the
* other side.
*
* WHICH DEFINITION, and it is the datasheet's: the Diodes table specifies
* fT at "VCE = -10V, IC = -10mA, f = 100MHz", i.e. the gain-bandwidth
* product measured at 100 MHz. That is what the 100 MHz minimum refers
* to, so that is what is locked. On the MJE15032/33, where ftest is
* 1 MHz, the same care changes a verdict rather than a digit - see
* NC-025.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* WHAT THIS MODEL DOES NOT HAVE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
*
* NO FLICKER NOISE: no KF, no AF anywhere in the line. Same gap as the
* two MJE models, the 1N4148, the LS350, the THAT320 vendor models and
* the hand-written placeholders - in this repo ONLY models/jfet/lsk489.lib
* has 1/f noise. NC-004 stays open for this reason, and any noise figure
* computed with this device is a floor without flicker, which must be
* written next to the number rather than left implicit.
*
* There is not a single SPICE magnitude suffix in the model line (every
* value is exponent form or a plain decimal), so the "1M is megohm in
* KiCad and milliohm in SPICE" trap of docs/limitations.md #13 has
* nothing to bite on here. Written down because this is where a later
* reader would come looking.
*
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
* BELOW THIS LINE: THE VENDOR FILE, BYTE FOR BYTE
* ------------------------------------------------------------------
